<description>
The function `gf_sc_scene_update` updates the scene of a compositor. It can be used to execute scripts or commands to modify the scene.
</description>

<requirements>
<requirement>
The `compositor` argument must be a valid pointer to a `GF_Compositor` object. This can be achieved by calling `load_compositor` with a valid `GF_Filter` pointer, which will initialize the global `compositor` variable.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `com` argument must be a non-NULL, null-terminated string. The function checks for a NULL `com` and returns `GF_BAD_PARAM`.
</requirement>
<requirement>
If the `type` argument is "application/ecmascript", the `com` argument should be a valid ECMAScript. This is because the function will attempt to execute the string as a script.
</requirement>
<requirement>
If the `type` argument is NULL, the `com` argument can be a command string starting with "gpac ", "add ", or "splice ". This is because the function parses these commands to modify the scene.
</requirement>
</requirements>

